omx-dsp (0.34.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * ci, release: the dry run passes staging and the wave's channel-level to
    release.yml
  * release: a dry run dispatched off main in a wave reads that wave's
    channel, as ci.yml's jobs do
  * ci: the contract job fetches the omx-contract commit the channel records,
    not a tag
  * tools/installed-source.sh: the commit an installed package was built
    from, read from the channel, no tag assumed
  * curve-sabotage: slope-enum targets the slope check that now takes dB and
    dBPerOct
  * release: omx-dsp 0.34.5 (0.34.4 to 0.34.5), a patch: a slope in dBPerOct
    is read as dB per octave
  * ci: Debian is trixie only
  * lint: the GCC 12.2 arm64 reduction check goes with bookworm
  * shapes/curve-io.schema.json: the request's unit words are the CURVE_UNITS
    ids
  * curve: a head filter's slope in dBPerOct, the PARAM_UNITS slope unit, is
    read as dB per octave
  * ci: the add-openmixer steps read the wave's devel channel and its base
  * fuzz-records: the eq records name the lines of omx_eq_design.h they now
    sit on
  * ci: the contract job's fedora:45 is a tool image, marked as the
    fedora-cells check asks
  * fuzz-records: the idelay records name the lines of omx_idelay.h they now
    sit on
  * fuzz-sabotage: fx-init-rate names the init-rate check at fuzz_fx.c:353,
    where it is now
  * release-promote-check: the binary-names plant is anchored on the line the
    promote job now has
  * release-arm-gate-selftest: the rpm job builds aarch64 beside x86_64
    (owner ruling 2026-11-26)
  * ci: no Debian bookworm cell (owner 2026-11-27: bookworm is dropped from
    the matrix)
  * generic-face: Migration item 6 is done, align and idelay through their
    descriptors (#185)
  * release 0.34.4: the entry describes the align and idelay descriptors, not
    instance faces (#185)
  * The hand-written align and idelay faces are removed (#185)
  * face-conformance: a required kernel has a face of either kind (#185)
  * align and idelay: descriptors for the generic face (#185)
  * generic-face: align and idelay go straight to the descriptor, as item 6
    says
  * align face: the engage-edge clear resets the cursors, it does not re-arm
  * release: omx-dsp 0.34.4 (0.34.3 to 0.34.4), a patch
  * generic-face: align and idelay have hand-written faces first (#185)
  * fuzz_fx: the align and idelay faces join the table, with their seeds
  * The align and idelay instance faces (#185)
  * face-conformance: the align and idelay instance faces are required

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Sat, 28 Nov 2026 19:57:23 +0000
